course: dictionary
lesson: 6662
title: Who is a nutritionist?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A nutritionist is a person who knows a lot about food and how it affects your health. You can use the words around a new word to work out its meaning. «Zoo kitchens prepare hundreds of meals a day, and nutritionists plan the right mix of food for each kind of animal.» The words plan, mix and food tell you the job is about choosing the right food.
explain: The clue «a zoo nutritionist who works rather like a doctor» tells you more. A doctor helps people stay healthy and get better, so a nutritionist helps animals, and people, stay healthy through food. Ask yourself: what job would fit this sentence? Then try your meaning in place of the hard word and check it still makes sense.
fact: Nutrition means the food we eat and how it helps our bodies grow and stay healthy.
fact: A nutritionist is a person who knows about nutrition and gives advice on healthy eating.
fact: Nutritionists work in hospitals, schools, sports teams and zoos.
fact: A zoo nutritionist plans meals for one kind of animal, or even one single animal.
fact: You can ask a nutritionist for help, but a nutritionist is not a cook: they plan what food is good for you.
exercise: «Zoo kitchens prepare hundreds of meals a day, and nutritionists plan the right mix of food for each kind of animal.» What do nutritionists do in this sentence? | Build the zoo kitchens | *Plan the right mix of food for each kind of animal | Feed the animals in the zoo | Look after the zoo's lions only
exercise: «...a zoo nutritionist who works rather like a doctor.» Which clue tells you a nutritionist looks after health? | hundreds of meals | *works rather like a doctor | zoo kitchen | single animal
exercise: A school nurse says, «Eat more vegetables and fruit for a healthy body.» Who would be the best person to ask for a plan of healthy meals? | A football referee | A gardener who only grows roses | A bus driver | *A nutritionist
test: What does a nutritionist know a lot about? | Cars and engines | Stars and planets | *Food and how it affects health | Music and songs
test: Why does the zoo nutritionist work rather like a doctor? | Because they work only at night | *Because they look after the animals' health through their food | Because they wear white coats | Because they treat broken legs
exam: Which sentence best explains what a nutritionist is? | A person who cooks dinner in a restaurant | *A person who knows a lot about food and health, and gives advice on healthy eating | A person who keeps animals safe in the wild | A person who sells tickets at a zoo
